recipes.caption:
Say NO to junk in snack boxes !!!

We all love eating junk food, and it’s OK, BUT ONCE IN A WHILE !

It’s not good for us and it’s definitely not good for our kids !

So here’s a list of ALL the brands we use for our snacks and our food 🤍

This is obviously not sponsored and I’m certain you’re going to love them all. And guess what, your kids won’t even be able to tell the difference, it’s THAT good. 😄

Thank me later 😉😄

Snacks - Cookies and Biscuits / Naturally flavoured Jowar puffs and Makhana / Fruit bites etc.

@snackadoodle_in
@nutriburp 
@thefarmersstore
@thecowboysfarm
@thewisefoodco
@aahar_foods
@thegrowinggiraffe
@littlefingers_food

Candy - THIS IS A GAME CHANGER -

we love ALL their products.
@mezmocandy
@fruitforest.in

Chocolate -

@lilgoodnessofficial - They have turmeric in their chocolate and it’s a prebiotic !!! So cool.

COOKIE BUTTER SPREAD by @thebetterbinge -
Makes great sandwiches for school - my kids can’t stop eating it. Think Lotus biscoff but 10 times cleaner and healthier. 

Our bread -

ONLY @gourmestan ! Bread, buns, pizza base, pav EVERYTHING ! 😄

Ice cream - @icebergorganicicecreams is just FAB !

Ghee and Clean dairy -

@thecowboysfarm
@gosaiagro 
@amritaha2ghee

Grains - Rice, Clean wheat etc.

@thecowboysfarm
@consciousfoodindia
@24mantraorganic
@organictattva
@pureandsure.in
@freshindiaorganics

Oil -
We very strictly use the wood pressed oils by @thecowboysfarm ! We use groundnut oil for basic Indian cooking.

Batters / Pancake mix / Roti and Dosa options etc.

@littlecherryfoods

Healthy pasta - we loooove these 

@nutrahelixindia
@thecowboysfarm
@slurrpfarm

Eggs -
@happy_hens_farm_india

Vegetables and Fruit -

@freshindiaorganics 
@zamaorganics
@thefarmersstore 
And of course our local farmers market.

Other than the above, we connect with a lot of clean bakers to make our cookies, muffins etc for school -

Topping that list is @fitnessbakery 

All the brands are fab and I urge you to share this with all your mom friends to try to ensure that all snack boxes coming to school are HEALTHIER THAN THE JUNK !
